    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1957650881941479732",
      "url": "https://x.com/destinationXIX/status/1957650881941479732",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/destinationXIX/status/1957650881941479732",
      "text": "History has already seen Gaza. It was called Manila, 1945.\n\nWhen U.S. forces liberated the Philippines, the Japanese army hid in churches, schools, hospitals - even used civilians as shields. The Americans faced a terrible choice: fight house to house and lose thousands of soldiers, or use overwhelming firepower to break the enemy. They chose the latter. Manila was reduced to rubble. 100,000 civilians were killed in a single month.\n\nAnd history judged it necessary. Because the world understood that the fault lay with Japan, which had turned a city into a fortress and civilians into pawns.\n\nNow look at Gaza. Hamas does the same - hides in hospitals, mosques, tunnels, and schools. They count on Israel’s humanity. They know Israel follows international law, values civilian life, and holds fire when it can. And they know that when Israel is forced to strike, Hamas can wave the bodies and scream “war crimes.” It’s the same strategy the Japanese used in Manila.\n\nThe only difference? In 1945, the Allies were praised for crushing tyranny. In 2025, Israel is condemned for doing the exact same thing.\n\nSo let’s be honest: if you cheered the Allies then but condemn Israel now, you’re not standing for justice - you’re standing for Hamas.",
